                            Under: $None,
                            Over: $None,
                            Outer: $None,
                            Neck: $None,
                        },
                    },
                ]>>
                <<ad _ad>>

            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Should I pull my pants down too so you can stare at my ass just as deeply?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> laughs as he turns back to look at you, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Maybe I can bend over too, give you something even better to look at?”</span> He continues to laugh as you turn away blushing, apologizing for staring. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m messing with you dude, calm your shit. I said before, I don’t care if you see it. It’s pretty nice, right? Better than most of the shitty tattoos people get here that are just random words in other languages.”</span> He snorts, wetting a rag as he washes the residue off his chest. <br>
            <br>
            You admit you are a bit surprised by the size and detail of it. You know he said it covered his back, but you didn’t actually think it would be this… covered. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, it’s pretty common back in Japan.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> says before adding, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, not common for everyday people. They kinda hate tattoos there, but it was common for the people I was around. I was in a sorta… gang back home. You know, band of brothers doing mischief and earning cash and all that.”</span> You can’t help but step a bit closer, so entranced by the honestly beautiful art on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span>’s back. It’s a bit weird to think that gangsters would get such pretty tattoos on their back. <br>
            <br>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha, gangsters is a weird thing to call them.”</span> He turns back around and throws the wet rag at you, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But I guess it makes sense outsiders would think the Yakuza is weird. It’s a cultural thing, they go back to like the 17th century. And this is called Irezumi, it used to be for spiritual protection and symbolism and stuff. Cherry blossoms show that life is short yet beautiful; I think that’s why they had me get it so young.”</span> He shrugs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hurt like a bitch, but it makes me the coolest kid in the bathhouse.”</span> <br>
            <br>
            You admit that the piece and even the story and symbolism behind it are kind of cool, though as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> mentions gangs and yakuza, you get a little worried. <span style="color:Yellow">Is he really mixed up with all that? Isn’t it a little dangerous?</span> <br>
            <br>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Calm down, all that’s in the past.”</span> He waves it off as he grabs a towel and wraps it around his upper body, planning to try to run to the locker room without being seen. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“My membership was kinda symbolic anyway. I could remove it, if I wanted, but that would hurt worse than getting it and be expensive as hell, so I’ll pass. Plus, it’s kinda cool. You gotta admit that much!”</span> He laughs, nudging you. This alleviates your worries a bit, <span style="color:Yellow">though you can’t help but wonder what sort of things <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> got up to back home.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Just wish they weren’t so anal about my hiding it all the time, swimming in a shirt is annoying as hell.”</span> He sighs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Whatever, I guess it makes sense. Last thing I want is to answer a bunch of idiots’ random questions every ten seconds. There’s only one idiot whose questions I’ll answer!”</span> He shoves you playfully with a smirk. <br>
            <br>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Welp, I’m going to get my gym shirt before I end up in detention. You can bounce if you want, doc should be done by the time I get back. I’ll catch you later.”</span> He gives you a sly wave as he runs off, the cherry blossoms on his back peeking out as the towel flutters up. You watch him as he rounds the corner and disappears before you start heading towards the exit of the school. <span style="color:LightGreen">You can’t help but feel closer to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> after learning about his tattoo and his past. He may be a bit of a punk, but deep down you get the feeling he likes being around you. It’s a nice feeling.</span> <br>
            <<socialChange "Kazu" 5 1>>
